{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Send back the ETag you were given as If-None-Match on the next request — if nothing changed, the server replies 304 Not Modified with no body, and you keep using what you already had.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">This validates freshness without guessing a cache TTL: the client always has data correct as of its last request, at a fraction of the transfer cost of a full re-download, because most responses become header-only 304s.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Handle 304 explicitly in your fetch layer before parsing a body — a naive .json() call throws on a real, body-less 304 — and pair ETag validation with Cache-Control: no-cache, which means "revalidate before use," not "don't cache."</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
